{
 "summary": "Updates the Windows codesigning script in contrib to pipe the private key passphrase to osslsigncode via standard input rather than passing it as a command-line argument. This prevents the signing passphrase from appearing in process listings on the signing machine.",
 "problem": "The Windows detached signature creation script passes the private key passphrase via osslsigncode's -pass argument. This exposes sensitive signing passphrases to other processes on the host via process tables and ps.",
 "evidence": [
  "Issue #36651 reports: 'contrib: detached-sig-create.sh passes the signing passphrases as arguments'",
  "PR description notes: 'osslsigncode -pass places the key passphrase in the process arguments, so ps can read it. So instead, pipe it to -readpass -, which reads it from stdin (osslsigncode 2.9+, the Guix codesign manifest uses 2.14).'"
 ],
